---
const columns = [
  {
    heading: 'Reads',
    tone: 'emerald',
    note: 'Free, repeatable and safe to run as often as a skill likes.',
    items: [
      'Holdings, with your own price anchors and target allocation on each',
      'Trade and dividend counts, and the summary totals per financial year',
      'Which years of the funds statement are on record, and which are missing',
      'Net contribution, itemised charges and the money-weighted return',
      'Saved valuations, their names and the quarter each speaks for',
      'Stock lists, research boards, screening verdicts and stock search',
      'When each kind of data was last uploaded, per trading account',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Writes',
    tone: 'amber',
    note: 'Checked before anything is stored, so a rejected write leaves the account untouched.',
    items: [
      'Holdings, tradebooks, dividends and the funds statement',
      'DCF and reverse DCF valuations, their notes and their quarter',
      'Stock lists and target allocation across the book',
      'Screening verdicts of study, track or reject',
      'Research boards, their columns and their cards',
      'Stock story videos to the Margin YouTube channel',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Closed to a token',
    tone: 'navy',
    note: 'Reserved for you, signed in to the Margin app.',
    items: [
      'Clearing holdings, dividends or a year of the ledger',
      'Deleting a research board',
      'Reading your funds statement row by row',
      'Reading dividends payout by payout or stock by stock',
      'The dashboard the web app reads for itself',
    ],
  },
];

const tones = {
  emerald: 'border-emerald-400/25 text-emerald-400',
  amber: 'border-amber-400/25 text-amber-400',
  navy: 'border-border text-muted',
};
---

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {columns.map((column) => (
    <div class={`rounded-xl border bg-navy-800/30 p-6 ${tones[column.tone as keyof typeof tones].split(' ')[0]}`}>
      <p class={`text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 ${tones[column.tone as keyof typeof tones].split(' ')[1]}`}>
        {column.heading}
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted/70 leading-relaxed mb-5">{column.note}</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5">
        {column.items.map((item) => (
          <li class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  ))}
</div>

<p class="text-xs text-muted/70 leading-relaxed mt-4">
  Two operations need a privilege beyond the token itself: generating quick stories and
  publishing a video to the channel. An account without the privilege gets a refusal that names
  it, and no token can grant itself one.
</p>
